# M1: an explicit call of a nonreturning callable has no result to pass to an int formal.
# It is not a reference expression selected by the receiving type; the bare name s would be a reference.
# Preserve the positive reference transport and explicit-call cases in unit_callable_nullary_forms.
# The bare-reference/int mismatch is separately pinned by unit_value_call_sub_refused.
# Current book #callables: evaluate an explicit call, then admit its result (if any).
int: y 0

sub: s ()
    y: 3
end: s

fn: g (int: n) int
    return: n
end: g

g(s())
return
